  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Section 3.9 of the Fedora Specification defines a new interaction pattern for external content.  The Fedora 4.x interaction is defined here: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/External+Content"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/External+Content",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ".  In a short the external content handling interaction  is triggered via the use of a special variation of the ContentType header.  The new interaction, defined in ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://fcrepo.github.io/fcrepo-specification/#external-content"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://fcrepo.github.io/fcrepo-specification/#external-content",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " , uses a link header instead. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Building on ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2748,"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2748,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " the task here is to add support for proxying an external binary (LDP-NR) content, ie using in a PUT or POST with the following header: ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Link: <",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://example.com/external/content/file"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://example.com/external/content/file",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "> ;",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "rel=\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora.info/definitions/fcrepo#ExternalContent"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora.info/definitions/fcrepo#ExternalContent",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\";",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "handling=\"proxy\";",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "type=\"text/plain\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If there is no type attribute, use the media type obtained when accessing the external content via the specified scheme (e.g. the Content-Type header for external content accessed via http).  Otherwise use default media type (application/octet-stream).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When serving requests for the the newly created resource, servers should use the recorded location and mime type from the above header to deliver the content via a proxied connection.  This ticket will be considered complete when support for http and https resources is complete.  Ie no need to support local files - this functionality is covered in ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2750"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2750",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
